  -- Mutant of the lemma `insert_then_remove_restores` (VOS04 5.6, `vos-link check-contract`): the model `abs_insert` of
  -- contract.part with one deliberate fault, which the lemma must catch: insert always sets thread 0, whatever thread it was asked for.
  -- It replaces the model of the same name by span; the tool refuses the mutant if the lemma still holds.
  model abs_insert(m: Ready, t: U8) -> (Upd, Ready) = (
    if t >= 8u8 then (OutOfRange, m)
    else (if mem(m, t) then (Unchanged, m) else (Changed, put(m, 0u8, true))))
